WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:08.951
A computer scientist writes the
programs a whole industry runs on.

2
00:00:09.171 --> 00:00:13.908
Service robots bring your parcel,
drive the train and help in hospitals.

3
00:00:14.408 --> 00:00:18.309
A computer scientist studies
how computers solve problems.

4
00:00:18.529 --> 00:00:23.219
Then they build the program that
does it. Every industry has problems.

5
00:00:23.439 --> 00:00:27.480
In a hospital, they build the
system that holds patient records.

6
00:00:27.700 --> 00:00:31.508
It keeps every record safe, and
finds the right one in a second.

7
00:00:31.728 --> 00:00:36.743
On a farm, their program reads soil
sensors and waters the dry fields.

8
00:00:37.243 --> 00:00:40.587
In a bank, they design the
encryption that keeps money safe.

9
00:00:40.807 --> 00:00:44.940
In a games studio, computer
scientists write the game itself.

10
00:00:45.160 --> 00:00:50.733
At a weather station, a model turns millions
of readings into tomorrow's forecast.

11
00:00:50.953 --> 00:00:55.040
You might think they only work at
computer companies. They do not.

12
00:00:55.260 --> 00:01:00.739
They work wherever a problem can be
solved by a program. That is everywhere.

13
00:01:01.239 --> 00:01:05.837
A service robot does a job for
people. Most do not look like people.

14
00:01:06.057 --> 00:01:11.769
Most are boxes on wheels, or arms, or
trains. A program controls each one.

15
00:01:11.989 --> 00:01:15.751
A delivery robot rolls along
the pavement with your shopping.

16
00:01:15.971 --> 00:01:19.314
It crosses at the lights,
and it stops at your door.

17
00:01:19.534 --> 00:01:24.271
A drone flies a parcel to an island.
A warehouse robot fetches your order.

18
00:01:24.771 --> 00:01:28.765
Some service robots move people.
That work is public transport.

19
00:01:28.985 --> 00:01:33.258
A driverless train runs the
airport shuttle. It has no driver.

20
00:01:33.478 --> 00:01:37.193
A self-driving shuttle bus
steers slowly round a park.

21
00:01:37.413 --> 00:01:42.150
In a hospital, a robot carries
medicines from the store to the ward.

22
00:01:42.370 --> 00:01:47.571
A surgical robot holds instruments steadier
than any hand. That is health care.

23
00:01:48.071 --> 00:01:53.504
Every service robot is a control
system. It senses, decides and acts.

24
00:01:53.724 --> 00:01:57.347
Cameras and a distance sensor
see the pavement and the people.

25
00:01:57.567 --> 00:02:03.604
The program decides. If a person is
close, stop. If the light is green, cross.

26
00:02:03.824 --> 00:02:07.307
A computer scientist wrote
every one of those rules.

27
00:02:07.527 --> 00:02:12.775
Then the motors act. Round and round in
a forever loop, until the job is done.

28
00:02:13.275 --> 00:02:17.501
A computer scientist builds
the programs an industry needs.

29
00:02:17.721 --> 00:02:21.993
Service robots deliver parcels,
move people and help in hospitals.

30
00:02:22.213 --> 00:02:27.043
Every one of them senses, decides
and acts. That is a control system.

31
00:02:27.263 --> 00:02:31.907
Wherever you go, ask what program
is working there. Someone wrote it.
